OHOS: the NDK libc++ has no ranges algorithms (std::__n1::ranges::any_of and
ranges::min_element are missing), so spell the same predicates with the
classic iterator forms. Behaviour is unchanged: the min_element comparisons
apply the same projection the ranges overload used.
diff --git a/snow_shot/src/presentation/ocr/screenshotocrtextlayout.cpp b/snow_shot/src/presentation/ocr/screenshotocrtextlayout.cpp
